 and coach statues; stay outside unless you have tour access.","short_summary":"An exterior campus landmark honoring Alabama football championships.","evidence_claim":"UA’s visitor guide says the Walk of Champions outside Bryant-Denny Stadium includes championship-team relief tributes and statues of championship-winning coaches.","source_url":"https://stories.ua.edu/visitors-guide/","source_title":"Campus Visitors Guide | The University of Alabama","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The UA visitor guide identifies the exterior Walk of Champions as free and open to the public.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ua-saban-field-bryant-denny-stadium","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"Saban Field at Bryant-Denny Stadium","title":"Finish at Bryant-Denny Stadium","subtitle":"920 Paul W. Bryant Dr. • Saturday afternoon","notes":"End the campus loop at the stadium exterior, then decide whether a separately scheduled tour fits your plans; do not assume field or interior access.","short_summary":"A major on-campus stadium and recognizable closing landmark.","evidence_claim":"UA’s visitor guide identifies Saban Field at Bryant-Denny Stadium as an on-campus facility and says stadium tours are sold online rather than available as walkups.","source_url":"https://www.ua.edu/wp-content/uploads/UA-Campus-Visitors-Guide-2025.pdf","source_title":"Campus Visitors Guide 2025 | The University of Alabama","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-01-01","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Exterior viewing is the conservative option. The guide says tours require online purchase and that walkups are not accepted.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ua-presidents-mansion","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"President's Mansion","title":"Close with the President’s Mansion","subtitle":"The Quad • Sunday morning","notes":"Circle back through the Quad to view this Greek Revival landmark from public outdoor areas and use it as a final reference point before leaving campus.","short_summary":"A historic UA landmark with nearly two centuries of campus presence.","evidence_claim":"UA describes the President’s Mansion as a Greek Revival home built in 1841 that survived the Civil War and has housed university presidents for nearly two centuries.","source_url":"https://stories.ua.edu/profile-of-excellence-2025-2026/index.html","source_title":"Profile of Excellence 2025–2026 | The University of Alabama","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"View the exterior from public areas; no interior access is implied by the source.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
